Reference:
Title	Gene expression profile and pathogenicity of biofilm-forming Prevotella intermedia strain 17
Author	Yamanaka T, Furukawa T, Matsumoto-Mashimo C, Yamane K, Sugimori C, Nambu T, Mori N, Nishikawa H, Walker CB, Leung KP, Fukushima H
Journal	BMC Microbiology
Year	2009
Volume	9
Issue	1
Page	11
Pubmed ID	19146705

Protocol:
Name	PI-array design
Description	To create a whole-genome microarray for P. intermedia strain 17, 30 perfect-matched and 30 miss-matched 24-mer probes were designed for all putative open reading frames (ORFs) (2,816 ORFs/array) from a whole genome sequence of P. intermedia strain 17 on the Institute for Genomic Research data base (TIGR: http://cmr.tigr.org/tigr-scripts/CMR/ CmrHomePage.cgi) using a Maskless Array Synthesizer (NimbleGen Systems Inc., Madison, WI, USA).

Name	PI-growth condition
Description	Grown in the enriched-TSB: trypticase soy broth (TSB; BBL Microbiology Systems, Cockeysville, ND) supplemented with 0.5% yeast extract , hemin (5 mg/l), L-cystine (400 mg/l) and vitamin K1 (10 mg/l) anaerobically in an anaerobic chamber (ANX-3, Hirasawa, Tokyo, Japan) at 37&deg;C in a 5% CO<sub>2</sub>, 10% H<sub>2</sub>, 85% N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere for 12 h.

Name	PI-labeling protocol
Description	Total RNA (12 &micro;g) was primed with random primer (Invitrogen, Tokyo, Japan), and cDNA was synthesized with reverse transcriptase (Superscript II, Invitrogen). The resulting cDNA was fragmented with DNase I (Promega, Madison, WI, USA) and biotin labeled using terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase (Promega).

Name	PI-extraction protocol
Description	Total RNA samples were extracted from 12 h cultures of strains 17 and 17-2 using RNeasy Midi Kit (QIAGEN, Tokyo, Japan) according to the manufacturer&#8217;s protocol.

Name	PI-pooling protocol
Description	Frozen stock in water at -80&deg;C

Name	PI-hybridization protocol
Description	Biotin-labeled samples were hybridized onto the strain 17 microarray at 45&deg;C for 16-20 h using NimbleGen&#8217;s Hybriwheel Hybridization chambers (NimbleGen Systems Inc.).

Name	PI-scanning protocol
Description	Hybridized-microarray slides were imaged with a high resolution array scanner (GenePix 4000B Microarray Scanner, Molecular Devices Corp., Sunnyvale, CA, USA) and the fluorescent signal intensities from each spot were quantified using NimbleScan Software (NimbleGen Systems Inc.).

Name	PI-immage analysis protocol
Description	Hybridized-microarray slides were imaged with a high resolution array scanner (GenePix 4000B Microarray Scanner, Molecular Devices Corp., Sunnyvale, CA, USA) and the fluorescent signal intensities from each spot were quantified using NimbleScan Software (NimbleGen Systems Inc.).

Name	PI-normalized protocol
Description	The data set was normalized by means of Robust Multi-chip analaysis algorithm.

Name	PIPLA-growth condition
Description	Prevotella intermedia strain 17 was cultured in enriched trypticase soy broth at 37&deg;C for 12 hrs anaerobically.

Name	PIBIO-growth condition
Description	Prevotella intermedia strain 17 was cultured on anaerobic blood agar plates at 37&deg;C for 12 hrs anaerobically.

