Array design text field:
Field	Description
PROBE_DESIGN_ID	This a unique, composite key consisting of the DESIGN_ID, ROW_NUM and COL_NUM.
CONTAINER	Probes are arranged in a variety of ways during the design process. To distinguish sets of probes, either physically or informatically, the probes are arranged in different containers. This column holds that name, often used during data analysis.
DESIGN_NOTE	A comment field suitable for placing information necessary for data analysis, for instance if you want to analyze sets of probes and/or genes together that don’t separate out using SELECTION_CRITERIA, CONTAINER, PROBE_CLASS or other information.
SELECTION_CRITERIA	For most standard designs, this field will contain some information about how the probe was selected for inclusion on the array.
SEQ_ID	The NimbleGen sequence identifier. Used to group the probe pairs together to generate average difference values. A SEQ_ID is a 17 character string that looks like: HSAP0001S00001834 The first four letters (HSAP) are the species code. The next four characters (0001) are the sequence build number. The ‘S’ is the designator for sequence (so there’s no confusion with the similar looking PROBE_IDs) The last eight digits are the unique sequence number within the sequence build
PROBE_SEQUENCE	The DNA sequence synthesized on the array
MISMATCH	The number of mismatches in the PROBE_SEQUENCE. Generally 0 (for the perfect match probe) or 2 (for the corresponding mismatch probe).
MATCH_INDEX	Integer number that ties probe pairs together. Using the combination of MATCH_INDEX and MISMATCH you can retrieve and distinguish the members of the probe pair. Many controls have a MATCH_INDEX of ‘0’ since they are not paired with a mismatch probe.
FEATURE_ID	A unique number used to tie together multiple features that compose a larger entity called a feature cell. For 4:9 format, the four individual features that comprise the larger feature cell will all have the same FEATURE_ID
ROW_NUM	The Y coordinate of the feature within the CONTAINER holding the feature.
COL_NUM	The X coordinate of the feature within the CONTAINER holding the feature.
PROBE_CLASS	Experimental or Control. Useful for queries where you want to pull out only certain classes of probes.
PROBE_ID	The NimbleGen probe identifier. A PROBE_ID is a 17 character string that looks like: HSAP00P0001724033 The first four letters (HSAP) are the species code. The next two digits designate the mismatch method. ‘00’ means no mismatch. ‘01’ is the standard two mismatches at 25% and 50%  (positions 6 and 12 from the 5’ end in a 24mer). The ‘P’ is the designator for probe (so there’s no confusion with the similar looking SEQ_IDs) The last ten digits are the probe number.
POSITION	When populated, this contains the position of the probe within the parent sequence
DESIGN_ID	This is the NimbleGen identifier for the design.
X	The absolute X coordinate of the feature on the array
Y	The absolute Y coordinate of the feature on the array

